exports[`extraction snapshots of ten recorded pages > 01-news-article.html 1`] = `
{
  "author": "Jane Doe",
  "bodyHtml": "<p>By Jane Doe</p>
<p>City planners in Example Town approved a new cycling network on Tuesday, adding forty kilometres of protected lanes over the next three years.</p>
<p>The plan, drafted after two years of public consultation, links the railway station with the university campus and the riverside business district.</p>
<p>Officials said the first segment, along Harbour Road, will open next spring, while the remaining routes depend on a regional grant that is still under review.</p>
<p>Local shop owners were divided: some welcomed the extra foot traffic, others worried about losing parking spaces in front of their stores.</p>
<p>The council will publish detailed maps and a construction timetable on its website before the end of the month.</p>
",
