{
  "author": null,
  "bodyHtml": "<p>Repot a plant when roots grow through the drainage holes or circle the bottom of the pot. Spring is the best time, because the plant is entering its growing season.</p><p>Choose a new pot only two to five centimetres wider than the old one, with drainage holes. Too large a pot holds extra water and can rot the roots.</p><p>Water the plant a day before, ease it out, loosen the roots gently, and set it at the same depth in fresh potting mix.</p>",
  "bodyText": "Repot a plant when roots grow through the drainage holes or circle the bottom of the pot. Spring is the best time, because the plant is entering its growing season.
Choose a new pot only two to five centimetres wider than the old one, with drainage holes. Too large a pot holds extra water and can rot the roots.
Water the plant a day before, ease it out, loosen the roots gently, and set it at the same depth in fresh potting mix.",
